WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.101 --> 00:00:01.700
(whimsical music)

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:04.010
- [Host] Over two billion
cups of coffee are consumed

00:00:04.010 --> 00:00:08.550
every day, and it take a lot
of people to make just one cup.

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:11.510
One man went on a quest to
figure out what it's like

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:13.693
to thank each and every one of them.

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:21.990
A.J. Jacobs is a writer
who lives in New York City.

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:24.060
- Hi, I'm A.J.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:25.210
- [Host] And he's the first to admit

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:26.883
he can be a bit of a grouch.

00:00:26.883 --> 00:00:29.870
- [A.J.] My default state is grumpiness.

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:33.330
I am very good at noticing
all the things that go wrong.

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:36.160
- [Host] So to make a change,
he started giving thanks

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:37.370
during dinner.

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:40.720
- [A.J.] I would say thank you to everyone

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:42.420
who helped make my meal.

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:43.650
- [Host] Until one night.

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:45.930
- [A.J.] My 10-year old son
was like, you know, Dad,

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:47.370
those people can't hear you.

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:48.410
If you really cared,

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:51.200
you would go and thank
these people in person.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:53.220
And that's when the light bulb went off.

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:55.040
- [Host] He decided to
hone in on something

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:57.640
he knew he took for granted every day:

00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:59.523
- [A.J.] My morning cup of coffee.

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:02.210
- [Host] Over the next 12 months,

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:04.890
A.J. set out to thank every
single person who had even

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:07.600
the smallest role in
his morning cup of joe.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.350
First, it was his local barista,

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:11.910
the roaster, and the coffee shop sourcer.

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:13.840
- [A.J.] Whenever I thanked one person,

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.810
they would say, "Well,
I couldn't do my job

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:17.190
"without this person."

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:20.100
So one person led to
another, led to another,

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:21.340
led to another.

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:23.260
- [Host] He ventured outside the city,

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:25.020
and eventually the country.

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:27.760
- [A.J.] I thanked the folks
who provide electricity

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:31.690
to the coffee shop, the
engineers who provide the water,

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:34.860
the people who make the steel, the farmer

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:38.090
and the importer, the truck driver,

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:39.740
the person who paved the road,

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:43.390
even the woman who painted
the yellow lines in the road

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:46.160
so that my coffee beans
could safely arrive

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:47.370
at my coffee shop.

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:50.960
I remember, I called the
woman who does pest control

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:53.950
for the warehouse, and I said,
"I know this sounds strange,

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:56.770
"but I want to thank you
for keeping the insects

00:01:56.770 --> 00:01:58.000
"out of my coffee."

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.400
And she said, "Well,
that does sound strange,

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:01.870
"but, thank you."

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:05.040
You know, I don't get a lot
of appreciation in my job.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:07.940
- [Host] All in, A.J. ended
up thanking over 1,000

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:10.770
different people, and while
most were pleasantly surprised

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:13.973
by his gratitude, it's A.J.
who benefited the most.

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:17.750
- [A.J.] The experience
has made me grateful

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:20.390
for the hundreds of things
that go right every day

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:22.610
as opposed to the three
or four that go wrong.

00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:25.080
I tell my friends that they should try

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:27.950
these gratitude trails themselves.

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:30.220
They could just be small gestures,

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:33.160
looking someone in the eye,
the cashier at the drugstore.

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:35.700
It could be sending a
quick note to the designer

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:37.060
of a logo you love.

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:40.310
I will tell you that it
will make your life better.

00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:42.890
It's changed the way I live my life.

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:46.057
(glittering flourish)

